# Level 1-08: Double Hold, Long Way Home — the World 1 capstone. Same "two ghosts each
# hold one plate, final self walks through unencumbered" pattern as 1-04, but the spine
# is longer and there's a Hazard decoy branch along the way — a confidence check before
# World 2 that pulls together recording, ghost replay, AND-gated cooperation, and hazard
# awareness all at once.
#
# Trace (spine at x=5, spawn (5,0), goal (5,11), door (5,10)=door:and:a+b):
#   Branch to plate A: (5,2)-(4,2)-(3,2)-(2,2). Branch to plate B: (5,5)-(6,5)-(7,5)-(8,5).
#   Branch to hazard H (decoy, off the solution): (5,7)-(4,7)-(3,7)-(2,7). All three are
#   dead ends reachable straight off the spine, each isolated from the rows above/below it
#   (checked: the rows immediately above and below each branch row are plain single-tile
#   spine with walls to both sides, so no branch connects to anything but the spine).
#   Loop 1 (recorded, -> ghost1): tick1 (5,1), tick2 (5,2), tick3 (4,2), tick4 (3,2),
#     tick5 (2,2)=A. Plate A activates at tick5 (occupancy). Loop runs its full
#     LOOP_SECONDS timer; ghost1 spawns, holding A forever after (idle past tick5).
#   Loop 2 (recorded, -> ghost2; ghost1 already replaying and back on A by tick5): live
#     player tick1 (5,1), tick2 (5,2) [passes the A junction without turning], tick3
#     (5,3), tick4 (5,4), tick5 (5,5), tick6 (6,5), tick7 (7,5), tick8 (8,5)=B. Plate B
#     activates at tick8. AND condition (a+b) now true from tick8 onward for the rest of
#     this loop and every loop after, since both ghosts idle-hold their plates forever.
#     Loop runs out its timer; ghost2 spawns.
#   Loop 3 (final, live, unencumbered): ghost1 holds A from tick5, ghost2 holds B from
#     tick8 (both replay identically every loop), so the AND door is open from tick8
#     onward before the player even sets off. Live player walks straight up the spine:
#     tick1 (5,1) ... tick7 (5,7) [passes the hazard junction without turning into it],
#     tick8 (5,8), tick9 (5,9), tick10 (5,10)=door (already open since tick8, no bump),
#     tick11 (5,11)=goal. Level complete at tick11 of loop 3.
#   The hazard at (2,7) is reachable (spine (5,7)->(4,7)->(3,7)->(2,7)) for a curious
#   player, but neither ghost's recorded path nor the final live path ever detours there.
#   Total: 3 loops (matches MAX_TIMELINES:2, i.e. two ghosts plus the final live pass),
#   ~11 ticks in the solving loop.
NAME: 1-08 Double Hold, Long Way Home
WORLD: 1
LOOP_SECONDS: 22
MAX_TIMELINES: 2
PAR_LOOPS: 3
PAR_TICKS: 16
GRID:
#####G#####
#####D#####
#####.#####
#####.#####
##H...#####
#####.#####
#####...B##
#####.#####
#####.#####
##A...#####
#####.#####
#####S#####
LEGEND:
S=spawn G=goal A=plate:a B=plate:b H=hazard D=door:and:a+b
